        "question": {
          ":question/id": "c31a514b-7294-50d3-b62c-2377163397ff",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\mathbf{u}=\\langle -1,-3,-4\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle 4,1,-1\\rangle$. Give an exact answer.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Compute the cross product using a determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{u}\\times \\mathbf{v}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\-1 & -3 & -4\\\\4 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot (1))\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad-((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot (4))\\mathbf{j}\\\\&\\quad+((-1)\\cdot (1)-(-3)\\cdot (4))\\mathbf{k}\\\\&=\\langle 7,-17,11\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude gives the corresponding parallelogram area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM&=\\|\\mathbf{u}\\times \\mathbf{v}\\|\\\\&=\\sqrt{(7)^{2}+(-17)^{2}+(11)^{2}}\\\\&=\\sqrt{459}=3\\sqrt{51}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested shape is the parallelogram, so use the whole magnitude.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA&=M=3\\sqrt{51}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
