        "question": {
          ":question/id": "81362fbf-ddb7-5e46-ad07-428641004fda",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "The triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle x,2,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,3\\rangle$ has area $\\frac{\\sqrt{286}}{2}$. Given that $x<0$, find $x$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$x=${{field-1}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Compute the cross product using a determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{b}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\x & 2 & 0\\\\0 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=((2)\\cdot (3)-(0)\\cdot (1))\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad-((x)\\cdot (3)-(0)\\cdot (0))\\mathbf{j}\\\\&\\quad+((x)\\cdot (1)-(2)\\cdot (0))\\mathbf{k}\\\\&=\\langle 6,-3x,x\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the triangle area formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA&=\\frac{1}{2}\\|\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{b}\\|\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt{286}}{2}&=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{10x^{2}+36}\\\\\\sqrt{10x^{2}+36}&=\\sqrt{286}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth sides are nonnegative. Square and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x^{2}+36&=286\\\\10x^{2}&=250\\\\x^{2}&=25\\\\x&=\\pm 5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x<0$, choose $x=-5$. Check in the original area relation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA&=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{36+10(-5)^{2}}\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{286}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
